contentText:
Packed into&nbsp;the mixing room of a studio&nbsp;at&nbsp;Sony Music&nbsp;Group’s&nbsp;New York headquarters on a Tuesday in mid-July,&nbsp;about&nbsp;a dozen college students listened as&nbsp;five-time&nbsp;Grammy award-winning recording engineer&nbsp;and producer&nbsp;Ann Mincieli&nbsp;described the life and career&nbsp;lessons&nbsp;she’s learned working nearly every job there is in a studio.&nbsp;

“There’s a whole world,&nbsp;basically,&nbsp;behind the artist,”&nbsp;said&nbsp;Mincieli, who has worked with&nbsp;artists including Alicia Keys , Mariah Carey ,&nbsp; Drake &nbsp;and&nbsp; DMX , and now&nbsp;designs&nbsp;and runs&nbsp;studios for Sony Music.&nbsp;

